chunks.text:
[Sertao accordion riff]
{Instrumental. Start immediately with a memorable ORIGINAL rural northeastern modal accordion riff doubled by twangy electric guitar. Authentic prominent zabumba}
{and triangle baiao groove, dry earthy bass ostinato. No quotation of an existing song.}

[Viola and accordion dance]
{Instrumental. Introduce a completely new major pentatonic accordion melody answered by acoustic viola, bass anticipation and zabumba slaps. Electric guitar adds}
{rhythmic bite underneath. Keep the baiao groove foreground.}

[Modal sertao bridge]
{Instrumental. Clearly different darker Mixolydian melody with flat seventh and call-and-response between accordion and twangy guitar. Triangle subdivisions and}
{syncopated zabumba break, no generic snare chorus.}

[Electric baiao finale]
{Instrumental. Original virtuosic accordion solo trading short phrases with gritty guitar over energetic zabumba variations. Evolve the opening rural riff and}
{resolve through an in-tempo turnaround for looping.}
